{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:3461c4f78c8ac0f1","name":"Fixer","source":{"id":"source:reference-3461c4f78c8ac0f1","title":"Fixer","revision":19661,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T22:22:31Z","sha256":"5dd26eae649c2a66f70704f54bce55d44350b6f49572a3058dd5f4feea20bfec","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19661","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Fixer&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-3461c4f78c8ac0f1","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scum and Villainy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scum_and_Villainy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Sometimes you need something that isn't available. You might be on the run, unable to buy anything openly. You might need something the law doesn't want you to have, ranging from slaves to military-grade weapons to illegal drugs. Your need might be more service-oriented, such as wanting to hire a smuggler or needing a medic to patch up a friend without any questions. Sometimes it's just information you need, but you need to get it without leaving a calling card at an official archive, and without others knowing you asked for it. In short, you need a Fixer.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["At one time, Fixers were mechanics or data slicers who could find goods on ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Black Market"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Black_Market"},", off the grid. As the Republic grew increasingly corrupt, however, the term came to mean a contact who could find other contacts. In fact, few Fixers know how to \"fix\" anything but the problem of finding what others want. A few work as procurement officers for front line forces (who are often out of supplies during battle) or Rebel forces (who are often out of supplies, period). Most work for criminal syndicates or as freelance mercenaries, putting together people, goods, and services for a fee, making sure no one's the wiser. Fixers are common in cantinas and starports, but they require either an introduction (from someone they know and trust) or a hefty bribe (to make the risk of a new contact worthwhile) before they'll arrange anything more shadowy than a drink.\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Fixer Statistics (CL 7)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scoundrel"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scoundrel","referenceId":"reference:316d580fd4c35ecc"}," 4/",{"tag":"a","children":["Noble"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Noble","referenceId":"reference:190d375ec3483f8f"}," 3\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 3\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +7; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +10\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic, Bocce, Bothese, Durese, High Galactic, Huttese, Ryl, Sullustese\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 18 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 18), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 18, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},": 21; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dodge"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dodge","referenceId":"reference:9444f216899dc20b"},{"tag":